Notification Service Integration Guide
Version: 1.0.0 Backend Service: NotificationService Base URL: http://<your-gateway-or-service-url>:9010 
Authentication
All endpoints require a JWT Token.
●	Header: Authorization
●	Format: Bearer <your_jwt_token>
1. Real-Time Notification Stream (SSE)
Establishes a persistent connection to receive real-time updates.
●	Endpoint: /notifications/stream
●	Method: GET
●	Headers: Authorization: Bearer <token>
Important Implementation Note for React
The native browser EventSource API does not support custom headers (like Authorization). Since our backend requires the token in the header, you cannot use new EventSource().
Recommended Library: @microsoft/fetch-event-source
React Implementation Example:
import { fetchEventSource } from '@microsoft/fetch-event-source';
import { useState, useEffect } from 'react';

const useNotifications = (token) => {
  const [notifications, setNotifications] = useState([]);

  useEffect(() => {
    if (!token) return;

    const controller = new AbortController();

    fetchEventSource('http://localhost:9010/notifications/stream', {
      method: 'GET',
      headers: {
        Authorization: `Bearer ${token}`,
      },
      signal: controller.signal,

      onopen(response) {
        if (response.ok && response.status === 200) {
          console.log("SSE Connection established");
        } else if (response.status >= 400 && response.status < 500 && response.status !== 429) {
          // Client-side errors (like 401) - usually fatal
          console.error("SSE Connection failed:", response.status);
        }
      },

      onmessage(event) {
        // 1. Handle the initial connection message
        if (event.event === 'connected') {
            console.log("Server says:", event.data);
            return;
        }

        // 2. Handle actual notifications
        if (event.event === 'new_notification') {
            const newNotification = JSON.parse(event.data);
            setNotifications(prev => [newNotification, ...prev]);
            
            // Optional: Trigger a toast or badge update here
            // toast.info(newNotification.message);
        }
      },

      onerror(err) {
        console.error("SSE Error:", err);
        // You can implement retry logic here if needed, 
        // though the library handles basic retries automatically.
      }
    });

    return () => {
      controller.abort(); // Close connection on unmount
    };
  }, [token]);

  return notifications;
};

Events Emitted
1.	connected: Sent immediately upon connection. Data: "Connection established".
2.	new_notification: Sent when a real notification arrives. Data: JSON Object (see Notification Object below).
2. Fetch Notification History
Get a paginated list of past notifications.
●	Endpoint: /notifications
●	Method: GET
●	Headers: Authorization: Bearer <token>
●	Query Parameters:
○	page (optional): Page number (0-indexed). Default: 0
○	size (optional): Items per page. Default: 20
Response (200 OK)
Returns a Spring Data Page object.
{
  "content": [
    {
      "id": "a1b2c3d4-e5f6-7890-1234-56789abcdef0",
      "userId": "user-123",
      "message": "Your 'Add' request for Segment Code (SGM1) has been approved.",
      "isRead": false,
      "createdAt": "2023-11-12T10:15:30Z",
      "linkUrl": "/my-requests/history/12345",
      "sourceEventId": "outbox-event-uuid"
    }
  ],
  "pageable": {
    "pageNumber": 0,
    "pageSize": 20,
    "sort": { "sorted": true, "unsorted": false, "empty": false },
    "offset": 0,
